                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "724b9031-0463-4a1d-95cd-9a124705addd",
                        "entry_id": "68b90915-731a-3bff-9bdb-b7ed3177c48f",
                        "tags": [
                            "adverbial",
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "рукоположи́вши"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "36ca7745-c302-3067-93d2-8a9703ea22c5",
                        "entry_id": "68b90915-731a-3bff-9bdb-b7ed3177c48f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "церк. посвятить в священный чин диакона, иерея или епископа возложением рук высшего духовного лица на голову посвящаемого"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a23bf65-92fc-4cd0-a820-91892a313188",
                                "sense_id": "36ca7745-c302-3067-93d2-8a9703ea22c5",
                                "text": "Ему было за семьдесят лет, полжизни он провёл диаконом в большом селе «Елисавет Алексиевны Голохвастовой», которая упросила митрополита рукоположить его священником и определить на открывшуюся ваканцию в селе моего отца."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "582531f2-6977-4d24-9c8a-1c9e5956f4ad",
                                "sense_id": "36ca7745-c302-3067-93d2-8a9703ea22c5",
                                "text": "Наконец Борисова рукоположили во священника и оставили служить четвёртым священником в той же церкви при Речном вокзале, где он много лет служил в сане диакона."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1de74f3a-dc49-48cf-973a-2c044e5fd211",
                        "source_entry_id": "68b90915-731a-3bff-9bdb-b7ed3177c48f",
                        "source_sense_id": "36ca7745-c302-3067-93d2-8a9703ea22c5",
                        "target_lang_word": "ordain",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ordain",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "72b859ac-88e2-395f-bece-633907819a69",
                                        "entry_id": "c9486275-53d1-31f5-8c9d-5537924861ec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To prearrange unalterably."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23b3c4b1-15bf-48b8-999e-f35c1b2b48c4",
                                                "sense_id": "72b859ac-88e2-395f-bece-633907819a69",
                                                "text": "What if the Foot, ordain'd the duſt to tread, / Or Hand, to toil, aſpir'd to be the Head? / What if the Head, the Eye, or Ear repin'd / To ſerve mere Engines to the ruling Mind?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5507163d-a4ae-3f7b-9c7d-ed24711ac7ab",
                                        "entry_id": "c9486275-53d1-31f5-8c9d-5537924861ec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To decree."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e74c719-3f8a-4b43-8190-49c14ce53479",
                                                "sense_id": "5507163d-a4ae-3f7b-9c7d-ed24711ac7ab",
                                                "text": "On once more we swung, bumping uneasily along in the antique narrow-gauge coach, with gloomy woods and gathering night outside, shouts and songs (and quacks) inside—this was not at all the sort of train ordained by the logical strategists in Paris—then grinding to a stop at a mysterious halt which was no more than a nameboard in the pinewoods, without even a footpath leading to it, but nevertheless with a solitary passenger stolidly waiting."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1675e65d-d349-3462-92d2-92ccca371c43",
                                        "entry_id": "c9486275-53d1-31f5-8c9d-5537924861ec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To admit into the ministry, for example as a priest, bishop, minister or Buddhist monk, or to authorize as a rabbi."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "282b6f75-0ab4-351f-a56e-92e359c80eb4",
                                        "entry_id": "c9486275-53d1-31f5-8c9d-5537924861ec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To predestine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
